  "review": {
    "KG:KG-21": "Real native SQL/Grafx processing asserts the exact old/new owner queue set, moves a Card to another Spec, removes its last Spec binding, then replays both events. Registered child/parent rules leave the old owner and converge to the new owner without duplicates; final unlink empties the queried owned set. Both source Specs, their declarations and Card graph root remain.",
    "KG:KG-23": "With the consumer deliberately processed first, a Spec creates a Decision successor at generation+1. Staged causal work refreshes the Card to the successor's physical identity and declared source reference. Exactly two Decision generations remain, predecessor content is preserved, no placeholder appears, and repeat processing preserves physical links plus complete relationship multiset.",
    "atomicity": "Injected failure after actually writing the downstream Card queue row propagates before ACK: SQL rolls back that row, the Spec stays pending with the exact injected error, and graph compensation restores original Decision identities/content/generation and Card link."
  },
  "correction": "When a live Spec consolidation supersedes graph nodes, enqueue its current Cards and directly linked Bug proxies through public application_persistence/relational_effects ports, under the same UOW and graph fence before ACK. Board/Spec/origin filters bound the set. Deduplication and coalesce_active=True preserve active claims/paused work and exact rebuild membership. No new semantic event, Board sweep, queue ordering rule or best-effort post-ACK dependency.",
  "failure_disposition": [
    "endpoint-generation1: physical supports query did not cover the logical layout; diagnostic snapshot confirmed the initial relation. Switched the test oracle to the existing logical graph reader.",
    "endpoint-generation2: real stale endpoint reproduced on main37. SQL audit confirmed Card ACK before Spec supersedence; queue drained while Card still referenced generation 0.",
    "endpoint-generation3: positive generation, parent change, Decision history and real crash passed. Negative fixture ran only one fair-queue turn, stopping after Card before its injection point. Corrected the fixture to process the Spec in a second turn; endpoint-generation4 passed that exact case.",
    "Initial closure38 had only README matrix mismatches, with all eight budgets zero. Official renderer regenerated both fragments; rebuilt/proved final pair and closure38-final passed."
  ],
